    {
      "id": "fDPMd5Ik8QIZtYGu9hnIH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 351.17218047369147,
      "y": 612.9432072887289,
      "width": 927.7194213867188,
      "height": 475,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ag",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1813463235,
      "version": 871,
      "versionNonce": 2023761901,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786620320514,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What Kind of ratelimiter we are going to design?\n    Client Side Rate Limiter\n    Server Side Rate Limiter\nShould this work in the Distributed Env?\nDoes the RateLimiter reduces the the api based on the Ip address,UserId or other properties\nRateLimieter should be implemented in seperate code?\nwhat is the scale of the system? is this built for the startup or the big company?\nDo you need to inform the user what need to throttled?\n\nRequirements\n    Accurately limits the excessive requests\n    Low Latency\n    Little Memory\n    RateLimiter can be shared across mutiple servers\n    Exceptional Handling\n    High fault tolerance\n\nClient side rateLimiting is not feasible --> we can bypass this\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What Kind of ratelimiter we are going to design?\n    Client Side Rate Limiter\n    Server Side Rate Limiter\nShould this work in the Distributed Env?\nDoes the RateLimiter reduces the the api based on the Ip address,UserId or other properties\nRateLimieter should be implemented in seperate code?\nwhat is the scale of the system? is this built for the startup or the big company?\nDo you need to inform the user what need to throttled?\n\nRequirements\n    Accurately limits the excessive requests\n    Low Latency\n    Little Memory\n    RateLimiter can be shared across mutiple servers\n    Exceptional Handling\n    High fault tolerance\n\nClient side rateLimiting is not feasible --> we can bypass this\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
